This usually happens to me when I use a data.frame for my sample genotypes. R helpfully adds an ‘X’ in front of samples that start with numbers and replaces spaces and punctuation with ‘.’. Maybe check the sample IDs in your sample genotype file and crossinfo file, paying special attention to any that start with numbers or have punctuation in them.

